// E1 - a local's address stored through a non-local pointer, INSIDE a region.
//
// The escape rule for this has existed since before the seal era and refuses the
// identical store one line up, outside the region. The walker simply had no arm
// for a seal body, so it never descended into one and every escape diagnostic was
// unreachable there. Found by the address round, which is the fifth time a round
// has turned up something that was not its own. The store went through a ward
// field holding a pointer until a rune's element became a register (#240); the
// pointer is a parameter now, and the rule and the region are the same.
fn arm(out: **u16) {
    let l: [u16; 4] = [1 as u16, 2 as u16, 3 as u16, 4 as u16];
    seal { *out = &l[0]; }
}

fn main() { println(0); }
